{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And when it rested.</b> Written ובנחה, read ובנוחו." "<b>And when it rested, he said: Return.</b> On account of the One who dwells among the myriads of thousands of Israel." "<b>Myriads.</b> Forms missing a bet, as in ״כי ששת ימים עשה HaShem״, ״שבי אלמנה בית אביך״, and many more. Another interpretation: ״Arise, HaShem, and let Your enemies be scattered״ — this is the prayer of the road." "<b>Return, HaShem, [among] the myriads.</b> May it be Your will that the myriads and the thousands return to their place in number, and not a single person be missing from us." "<b>Return.</b> Like והשיבה, for example ״ושב HaShem את שבותך״, which is like והשיב (and He shall restore)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:20.701958737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}